cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite the paper (preferred-citation) and this repository."
title: "evae-dfn-bench-faces: data and code for 'Data-driven generative modelling of discrete fracture networks with geology-informed constraints'"
type: software
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
repository-code: "https://github.com/europdl23/evae-dfn-bench-faces"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Traced data and code of the paper. The traced data are the 2D end points of the fracture traces mapped on the bench
  faces of one open-pit wall, in sampling-window coordinates (50 sampling windows, 735 clipped traces), with the window
  grid and the fold definitions of the three hold-out tests. The code (training, generation, evaluation, side check,
  engineering inputs, sensitivity tests, figures) comes with its outputs: the trained enhanced variational autoencoder (EVAE) models, the
  fitted ADFNE and KDE baselines, every generated realisation with its seed, and the tables and figures of the paper.
  Code is MIT-licensed; data, models, realisations, tables and figures are CC BY 4.0. Photographs, orthophotos, the
  photogrammetric model and 3D or mine-grid coordinates are not released.
keywords:
  - discrete fracture network
  - fracture traces
  - generative modelling
  - variational autoencoder
  - rock mass characterisation
